    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0302" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg270"/>

                <head>125. Telegram From the Embassy in Poland to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d125-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Warsaw</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-09-25T18:00:00+02:00">September 25,
                            1958, 6 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>475. USUN for Lodge. Beam–Wang Talks. Today’s meeting one hour
                    45 minutes.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d125-f2"/>
                    Wang asked lead off to which I agreed and he read statement
                    covering same familiar ground he covered last meeting, adamantly rejecting
                    ceasefire, accusing US of ulterior motives and insisting on US withdrawal forces
                    from area could relieve tension, no significant alternative tone or language
                    from that adopted last meeting. I responded with brief rebuttal several specific
                    points, then read prepared statement based Department’s 329.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d125-f3"/>
                    Wang made vigorous rebuttal but said nothing new. Brief
                    further exchange brought meeting to close. I did not mention we would present
                    new draft next meeting as there seemed no necessity tip <pb facs="0303" n="271"
                        xml:id="pg271"/> our hand. Wang proposed Monday
                    afternoon. I countered with Monday morning as more convenient and we agreed on
                    Tuesday September 30, 10 a.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Beam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d125-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d125-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/9–2558. Secret; Niact; Limit Distribution. Received at 12:42 p.m.
                    Repeated priority to USUN and niact
                    Taipei.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f2" n="1" xml:id="d125-f2-content">
                <p>Beam sent a detailed report of the meeting
                    in telegram 477 from Warsaw, September 25. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.;</hi>
                    see Supplement)</p>
            </note>
